KG42.register("rules-e2f26fb351f6438cd0eb3979",{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R011","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local clearing price","process_stage":"pricing","market_meaning":"The local market clearing process determines the local electricity price. Scope: Electricity pricing in the proposed local energy market. In the reported transition-time case, synchronized demand-bid submissions for the same delivery time cause an increase in local market clearing prices. Scope: Reported transition-time simulation of the residential heat-pump LEM. Condition: Multiple prosumers plan to run their heat pumps simultaneously and submit bids for the same delivery time. The local auction uses uniform pricing. Scope: Pricing design of the proposed centralized two-sided local auction.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function pricing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","clearing.local","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R011-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"pricing.local","type":"implies","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R011-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E03"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R011-E002","source":"clearing.local","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R011-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Electricity pricing in the proposed local energy market. | Pricing design of the proposed centralized two-sided local auction. | Reported transition-time simulation of the residential heat-pump LEM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E03"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local market clearing process determines the local electricity price. Scope: Electricity pricing in the proposed local energy market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"In the reported transition-time case, synchronized demand-bid submissions for the same delivery time cause an increase in local market clearing prices. Scope: Reported transition-time simulation of the residential heat-pump LEM. Condition: Multiple prosumers plan to run their heat pumps simultaneously and submit bids for the same delivery time.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E03"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local auction uses uniform pricing. Scope: Pricing design of the proposed centralized two-sided local auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a so ute educt o o t e e e gy su p us s a ecause o t e lower solar radiation in winter. cl The compa","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"LEMs aim to provide advantageous electricity prices by facilitating lower local market prices for all participants. Energy buyers can save costs by using electricity cheaper than the retailer prices, while energy sellers can earn more money compared to direct sales to the retailer. These electricity prices are determined by the market clearing process."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p08-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"e pp y p gy, clearing prices in the LEM fluctuate in day time. It can be observed at that it drops s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Although the weighted average prices at night are all identical to the retailer’s supply price due to the lack of renewable energy, the market clearing prices in the LEM fluctuate in day time. It can be observed that it drops significantly once PV generation is abundant in transition time and summer. In summer, most bids are cleared at 1 cent/kWh in the middle of the day because of the sufficient supply of PV power and the lack of heat demand. In contrast, the market clearing prices in transition time fluctuate strongly. This stems from the diverse operation schedules of heat pumps. Once multiple prosumers plan to run their heat pumps simultaneously, they submit their bids in the LEM for the same delivery time, causing the increase in market clearing prices. When there is no heat demand, the market clearing prices drop to a low level. In winter, the situation is totally different. Owing to the high heat demand and low supply of PV power, electricity prices are always cleared at a high level. Even though some trading is completed at 5–6 cents/kWh, most are at 10 cents/kWh. Therefore, the cost-saving potential of the LEM for prosumers in winter is not obvious."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No design-selection or operational-decision variable is declared in R011's frozen graph. The only plausible candidate is an endogenous local clearing-price outcome, but C.1 did not declare such a variable and its optimization role/domain is not established by the attached support.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed coefficient, bound, or constant is attached to R011. The reported 1-10 cent/kWh values are simulation outcomes, not parameters of this pricing rule, and no source-defined parameter such as a price ceiling/floor is part of the frozen R011 evidence."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-matching","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","quote":"These electricity prices are determined by the market clearing process."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E03","quote":"Once multiple prosumers plan to run their heat pumps simultaneously, they submit their bids in the LEM for the same delivery time, causing the increase in market clearing prices."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","quote":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"54a47c30eddda24149cbc361ebc18adf85ff2d1e84fd3b8cb33744b0fbfd1ffb","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The attached source support is qualitative: C001 states that the local clearing process determines the local price, C002 reports a simulation observation about synchronized demand bids and higher clearing prices, and C003 states uniform pricing. A faithful mathematical expression for C001 or C003 would require a declared local clearing-price variable and an accepted-bid/demand-supply-curve structure, none of which is present in the frozen graph. B evidence remains unreviewed, so no expression, variable, parameter, domain, or coefficient is invented.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-C001","node_ids":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E002"],"rationale":"The existing links edge E002 supports the relation that the local clearing process determines the local price. No expression is added because the graph lacks a declared local clearing-price variable and a demand/supply-curve representation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-C002","node_ids":["bidding.demand","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E001"],"rationale":"The existing implies edge E001 records that synchronized demand-bid submissions are associated with higher local clearing prices. The attached source support is a qualitative simulation observation without a formula or quantified condition."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-C003","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Uniform pricing is a property of pricing.local only. No accepted-bid set, per-bid settlement price, or settlement-price node is present, so the uniform-price condition p_i = p_t^LEM for accepted bids cannot be faithfully written from this graph."}],"revision_requests":["Define or authorize a local clearing-price variable p_t^LEM for delivery time t, attached to pricing.local, with explicit unit and scope (LEM clearing price, not retailer fixed buy/sell price or excess-PV feed-in rate); R011 currently has no price variable and C.1 field notes state that typed variables are outside the draft.","If C001 is to be formalized as a demand/supply-curve intersection, add graph support for ordered demand bids, supply offers, and the market-operator/matching step, or explicitly confirm how pricing.local alone represents the intersection relation.","If C003 is to be formalized as uniform settlement p_i = p_t^LEM for accepted bids, add the accepted-bid or settlement-price object and any necessary edge; do not infer buyer/seller acceptance solely from existing E001/E002.","For C002, provide a source-supported price-change variable or baseline if a causal inequality is required; otherwise retain it as a qualitative simulation observation because the quotation gives no formula, coefficient, or quantified condition.","B evidence remains unreviewed. Candidate evidence v141-b-g01-e10 (demand/supply intersection) is not currently an evidence_id of any R011 constraint; C.1 should either attach it with explicit scope or exclude it before expression-level formalization."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
